# 🫁 Chest X-Ray Pneumonia Classification

### Convolutional Neural Network for Medical Image Classification
**Author:** Michał Mańkowski
**Dataset:** Chest X-Ray Images (Pneumonia) — Kaggle
**Stack:** Python, TensorFlow, Keras, Scikit-learn, Matplotlib

---

## 📌 Project Overview
This project uses a **Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)** to classify
chest X-ray images as either NORMAL or PNEUMONIA.
The model was trained on 5,216 images and tested on 624 images.

---

## 📊 Results

| Metric | Value |
|--------|-------|
| **Test Accuracy** | 82.21% |
| **Pneumonia Recall** | 0.78 |
| **Normal Recall** | 0.23 |

---

## ⚠️ Key Challenge — Class Imbalance
- **74% PNEUMONIA** vs **26% NORMAL** in training data
- Model is biased toward predicting Pneumonia
- In medical context **Recall > Accuracy** — missing a sick
  patient is more dangerous than a false alarm

---

## 🏗️ CNN Architecture
```
Input (150x150x3)
    → Conv2D(32) + MaxPooling
    → Conv2D(64) + MaxPooling
    → Conv2D(128) + MaxPooling
    → Flatten
    → Dense(512) + Dropout(0.5)
    → Dense(1) sigmoid → NORMAL / PNEUMONIA
Total parameters: 19,034,177
```

---

## 🗺️ OSEMN Framework

### 🔵 O — Obtain
- Downloaded Chest X-Ray dataset from Kaggle
- 5,216 training images | 624 test images | 16 validation images

### 🧹 S — Scrub
- Normalized pixel values to **0-1** range
- Applied **data augmentation**: rotation, zoom, horizontal flip
- Computed **class weights** to handle imbalance

### 🔍 E — Explore
- Visualized sample NORMAL vs PNEUMONIA X-rays
- Identified severe class imbalance (74% vs 26%)

### 🤖 M — Model
- Built 3-block CNN with Dropout regularization
- Used **EarlyStopping** — stopped at epoch 6/20
- Trained with **class weights** to balance learning

### 📊 N — Interpret
- Model achieves **82.21% accuracy** on unseen test data
- Strong **Pneumonia detection (Recall 0.78)**
- Identified class imbalance as main challenge

---

## 💡 What I Learned
- How to build and train a **Convolutional Neural Network**
- How to handle **class imbalance** in medical datasets
- Why **Recall matters more than Accuracy** in medical AI
- How **EarlyStopping** prevents overfitting

